cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the derived results, please cite both the archived software and the article."
title: "Carbon on the Hills, Green in the Alleys: analysis code and results for the spatial mismatch of canopy structure and green exposure in Taipei City"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-21
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Analysis code and reproducible outputs for a study of the spatial mismatch between
  canopy-structure carbon proxy (ΣH) and 500 m green-supply exposure (SAI) across the
  near-mountain–urban interface of Taipei City. Includes data auditing, canopy and
  accessibility indices, spatial autocorrelation and block inference, sensitivity and
  robustness checks, national township/county comparisons, CHMv2 validation against the
  street-tree census, and all figure generation scripts (PIL-based).
keywords:
  - urban green accessibility
  - canopy height model
  - spatial mismatch
  - spatial autocorrelation
  - Taipei City
  - near-mountain-urban interface
